//! The `mask-border-width` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the
//! width of an element's [mask
//! border](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-border).
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: relative to width/height of the mask border image area.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The width of the mask border is made equal to the intrinsic width or height (whichever is
//! applicable) of the corresponding `mask-border-slice`. If the image does not have the required
//! intrinsic dimension, the corresponding `border-width` is used instead.
//!
//! Grammar: <'border-image-width'>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-masking-1/#propdef-mask-border-width
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-border-width
